 case (map names per documented JaxMARL SMAX suite; to be verified against the pinned repo version before execution \u2014 see Section 9):\n\n  Tier / Map            Allies vs Enemies   Rationale\n  Small  / 5m_vs_6m      5 vs 6             canonical easy map, fast runs\n  Small  / 2s3z          2 stalkers+3 zealots small mixed unit types\n  Medium / 3s5z          3 vs 5             standard medium benchmark\n  Medium / 6h_vs_8z      6 vs 8             hard asymmetric case\n  Large  / 10m_vs_11m    10 vs 11           large-marine scale test\n  Large  / 2c64_40z      64 vs 40           extreme scale; JAX speedup claims strongest here; first candidate to drop if over budget\n\nEnvironment settings: JaxMARL default SMAX configuration (including the defaults documented in the JaxMARL paper, e.g., move-state/local-obs feature flags) for both algorithms; identical env config for both arms. Stochastic env steps ON. Env config YAMLs are pinned and archived alongside results.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n3. ALGORITHMS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u2022 PPO arm: JaxMARL IPPO baseline (baselines/IPPO/main.py), shipped per-map Hydra configs.\n\u2022 Q-Learning arm (primary): JaxMARL QMIX baseline (baselines/QMIX/main.py), shipped per-map configs. Optional secondary: VDN (same codebase, config switch).\n\u2022 Hyperparameters: DEFAULTS ONLY from the pinned JaxMARL version's per-map configs. No retuning. This is a deliberate fairness/feasibility trade-off (see Threats T3).\n\u2022 Version pinning: exact git commit hash of JaxMARL, plus versions of jax/jaxlib and CUDA, recorded in the run manifest. The repo is cloned once; a checksum of the tree is recorded.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n4. INDEPENDENT / DEPENDENT VARIABLES AND CONTROLS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u2022 IV: algorithm \u2208 {IPPO, QMIX} (+ optional VDN); Moderator: map (6 levels); nuisance: seed (5\u201310 levels).\n\u2022 DV1 (primary time): wall-clock seconds to reach the fixed per-map env-timestep budget (Table in \u00a76), JIT warm-up excluded from the primary figure but reported separately per run.\n\u2022 DV2 (secondary time): time-normalized AUC of normalized score vs. wall-clock hours, sampled at eval checkpoints.\n\u2022 DV3 (score): anchor-based normalized score at the budget (definition in \u00a75), plus learning curves of normalized score vs. env steps and vs. wall-clock.\n\u2022 Controls: same device, sequential runs (never concurrent), same eval protocol both arms, same env config, same commit, warm-up run per (algo, map) pair before timed runs, timestamps and device telemetry logged.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n5. METRIC DEFINITIONS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nScore metric: WIN RATE (assumption; see \u00a710 A6). Justification: SMAX inherits SMAC's win/loss episode outcome (\"all enemies defeated\" without timeout), win rate is the standard SMAC/SMAC-style benchmark metric, is bounded and comparable across maps, and is less sensitive to return-scale differences between algorithms than raw episode return. Raw episode return is logged but reported only as a sanity check, not as the primary score.\n\nNormalized score (per map m, per run, at a given checkpoint):\n  NS = clip( (WR \u2212 WR_random) / (WR_heuristic \u2212 WR_random), 0, 1 )\nwhere WR_random is the win rate of an untrained/random policy evaluated in the same harness (20+ episodes, same eval protocol), and WR_heuristic is the win rate of SMAX's built-in scripted/heuristic agent (e.g., \"independent\" attack-closest policy) under the same protocol.\n  Fallback: if a heuristic anchor is unavailable or degenerate (WR_heuristic \u2212 WR_random < 0.05) for a map, use min\u2013max normalization over the pooled observed range of both algorithms on that map, and flag the map's NS values as fallback-based in all figures.\n\nTraining-time accounting:\n  \u2022 Timed region: from the first post-compile training step to the step at which the cumulative env-timestep budget is reached, measured with explicit device synchronization.\n  \u2022 JIT warm-up (compilation) time recorded separately per (algo, map); excluded from the primary metric because it is a one-off, not per-sample cost; also reported as time-to-budget-inclusive-of-compile for transparency.\n  \u2022 Eval time is excluded from training time (it is protocol overhead, identical across arms) but logged.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n6. RUN MATRIX AND ESTIMATED COSTS (ESTIMATES ONLY \u2014 nothing run)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nPer-map env-timestep budgets and per-run wall-clock estimates (single modern data-center GPU, e.g., A100-class; ranges wide because they are pre-execution guesses derived from JaxMARL's reported throughput, NOT measurements):\n\n  Map          Budget (env steps)  Est. h/run (IPPO)  Est. h/run (QMIX)\n  5m_vs_6m     1M                  0.3\u20130.6            0.3\u20130.6\n  2s3z         2M                  0.5\u20130.9            0.5\u20130.9\n  3s5z         3M                  0.9\u20131.6            0.9\u20131.6\n  6h_vs_8z     3M                  1.0\u20131.8            1.0\u20131.8\n  10m_vs_11m   5M                  1.5\u20132.5            1.5\u20132.5\n  2c64_40z     5M                  3.0\u20136.0            3.0\u20136.0\n\nRun matrix (primary design): 2 algorithms \u00d7 6 maps \u00d7 5 seeds = 60 runs.\nEstimated totals (5 seeds, per map, both algorithms = 10 runs \u00d7 est. h/run):\n  5m_vs_6m \u2248 3\u20136 h; 2s3z \u2248 5\u20139 h; 3s5z \u2248 9\u201316 h; 6h_vs_8z \u2248 10\u201318 h; 10m_vs_11m \u2248 15\u201325 h; 2c64_40z \u2248 30\u201360 h.\n  TOTAL \u2248 72\u2013134 GPU-hours (~3\u20136 days of continuous single-GPU time), plus ~5\u201315 min compile warm-up per (algo, map) pair (12 pairs \u2248 1\u20133 h total) and eval overhead (~10\u201315% of training time).\n\nBudget tiers (feasibility analysis, since the GPU-hour budget is unstated):\n  Tier 1 (full, ~72\u2013134 GPU-h): all 6 maps, 5 seeds. Preferred.\n  Tier 1+ (~145\u2013270 GPU-h): 10 seeds instead of 5.\n  Tier 2 (+40\u2013120 GPU-h): adds VDN as the secondary Q-Learning arm (same matrix), answering the interpretation ambiguity empirically.\n  Tier 3 (degraded, ~45\u201375 GPU-h): drop 2c64_40z (\u221230\u201360 h); 5 maps \u00d7 5 seeds.\n  Tier 4 (minimal, ~35\u201355 GPU-h): drop 2c64_40z AND shorten large-map budgets 10m_vs_11m 5M\u21923M (\u22126\u201310 h); 5 maps, reduced budgets, 5 seeds.\n  CPU-only fallback caveat: JAX's headline speedups (and JaxMARL's claims) are GPU-dependent; on CPU the wall-clock comparison loses external validity and total cost explodes (likely 10\u00d7 or worse). CPU-only execution is NOT recommended; if forced, report it as a distinct, non-comparable condition and restrict conclusions accordingly.\n  Decision rule: if the budget allows < Tier 3, reduce seeds to 3 on the two largest maps first (flagged as low-power), rather than dropping the hard map.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n7. EVALUATION PROTOCOL (EXACT)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u2022 Cadence: evaluation every 50,000 env steps of training (20 checkpoints at 1M, 100 at 5M; final eval always at the exact budget).\n  Cadence is expressed in env steps (not wall-clock) so both arms get identical checkpoint alignment; the time-normalized AUC interpolates between checkpoints.\n\u2022 Per checkpoint: 32 evaluation episodes, greedy policy, deterministic eval env seeding (fixed eval-seed base per checkpoint, shared across algorithms and seeds), on the same device type as training.\n\u2022 Anchors (random policy, heuristic baseline) evaluated once per map with 100 episodes each, same protocol, before the run campaign.\n\u2022 Recorded per checkpoint: win rate, mean/std episode return, episode length, wall-clock timestamp, cumulative env steps.\n\u2022 Win rate is the primary score (\u00a75); return logged for sanity checks only.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n8. STATISTICAL ANALYSIS PLAN\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u2022 Per-map comparisons (5 seeds/arm):\n  \u2013 Score: final NS at budget; mean \u00b1 95% bootstrap CI (10,000 resamples over seeds); Welch's t-test or Mann\u2013Whitney depending on normality, with Holm correction across the 6 maps.\n  \u2013 Time: wall-clock to budget; mean \u00b1 95% CI; report the ratio IPPO/QMIX with CI (ratio is more interpretable than the difference).\n  \u2013 Time-to-threshold: first checkpoint where NS \u2265 0.8 of the heuristic anchor (or final NS if never reached); compared per map.\n  \u2013 Time-normalized AUC: computed by trapezoidal integration of NS vs. wall-clock hours; CI via seed-level bootstrap.\n\u2022 Aggregate: rliable-style IQM of NS across maps with stratified bootstrap (2,000 iterations); performance-profile and probability-of-improvement curves over wall-clock. LIMITATION (explicit): with only 6 maps, the aggregate is a descriptive summary of these maps, not a population-level inference over all SMAX tasks; per-map results carry equal weight in the narrative.\n\u2022 Effect sizes reported (Cohen's d or rank-biserial) alongside p-values; no dichotomous \"significant/not\" framing in the conclusions.\n\u2022 Pre-registration: run matrix, budgets, metric definitions, and analysis plan (this document) are fixed before any run; deviations logged.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n9. THREATS TO VALIDITY\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nT1 \u2014 Unverified repository details. The design workspace contained no JaxMARL source (only task.json; network disabled; jax/jaxmarl not importable). Map names, baseline entry points (baselines/IPPO, baselines/QMIX), config flag names, and heuristic-baseline availability are from documented knowledge of the public repo and its paper and were NOT verified here. First execution step: clone the pinned version and validate every path/config name cited above; revise the design doc if any artifact differs.\nT2 \u2014 Version drift. JaxMARL is actively developed; throughput and defaults change across versions. Mitigation: single pinned commit + dependency manifest; results stated as version-specific.\nT3 \u2014 Hyperparameter-default confound. Defaults-only means each algorithm's tuning state is whatever the JaxMARL authors chose per map; a gap could reflect tuning effort, not algorithmic merit. Mitigation: document all hyperparameters per arm; sensitivity note in the report; retuning explicitly out of scope.\nT4 \u2014 Hardware dependence of JAX speedup claims. Wall-clock conclusions are valid only for the declared GPU configuration; CPU-only execution would qualitatively change the comparison (see \u00a78 Tier caveat). Concurrent runs on one device would distort timing; sequential-only is a design constraint, not a preference.\nT5 \u2014 Q-Learning interpretation ambiguity. Results hold for QMIX (and optionally VDN), not for Q-learning in general; stated prominently in \u00a71 and in every results summary.\nT6 \u2014 Normalization anchors. Heuristic anchor quality varies per map; degenerate anchors trigger the min\u2013max fallback, which makes cross-map aggregation slightly less comparable (mixed normalization bases are disclosed per map).\nT7 \u2014 Compile-time treatment. Excluding JIT warm-up flatters both arms equally, but the relative share of compile time differs by map size; both figures (inclusive/exclusive) reported.\nT8 \u2014 Seed variability at 5 seeds. CIs on 5 seeds are wide for hard maps where win rate is near 0 or 1; conclusions on such maps will be reported as inconclusive rather than forced. 10-seed tier preferred.\nT9 \u2014 Budget truncation. Algorithms still improving at the budget get truncated NS values; learning-curve-at-budget is the primary score readout, and \"time-to-threshold\" analysis partially mitigates truncation bias.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n10. ASSUMPTIONS (proposed defaults, not task-fixed)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nA1. \"Q-Learning\" = QMIX (primary), VDN optional (resolution 1; prominent flag in \u00a71).\nA2. Fixed env-timestep budget is the primary time comparison; wall-clock AUC is secondary.\nA3. SMAX heuristic agent provides a valid anchor on all maps (fallback defined).\nA4. Defaults-only hyperparameters are acceptable (resolution 2).\nA5. 5 seeds minimum, 10 preferred (resolution 2); estimates in \u00a76 assume 5.\nA6. Win rate (not raw return) is the normalized-score input, per \u00a75 justification \u2014 flagged